# cutforge conventions

Canonical layout write-up: `knowledge/project-layout.md` (read it when creating projects).

## Repo layout

```
cutforge/
  knowledge/                 # team knowledge base (agents must consult)
  .cursor/skills/            # Cursor Agent Skills
  .cursor/rules/             # always-on project rules
  davinci/presets|templates  # shared Resolve assets
  projects/<live-name>/      # live projects only — no _template
    scenarios/
    timelines/               # .drt handoff
    configs/
    notes/                   # MEDIA.md, LOCKS.md
  skills/                    # pointer README → .cursor/skills/
```

- New project: follow `knowledge/project-layout.md` (mkdir tree + MEDIA/LOCKS). Do not invent a parallel structure.
- Do **not** commit source media, renders, Resolve cache, `.dra`, or local DB media.
- Scenario files may live next to source media outside git; keep paths in `notes/MEDIA.md`.

## Team timeline handoff

- Exchange cuts via **`.drt` only** → `projects/<name>/timelines/<slug>.drt`.
- Do not use FCPXML/AAF/EDL for normal cutforge collaboration (debug/external only).
- Skill: `.cursor/skills/timeline-drt-share/`. Draft commit messages — commit only when asked.
- After import: check offline clips; relink with user confirmation.

## Source media safety (disk)

- **Never** move, rename, overwrite, delete, or recompress source files on disk.
- Organize only inside DaVinci Resolve (bins, timelines, markers) via API/MCP.
- Import/relink only when the user asks; still do not alter originals.
- Proxies/renders/exports → only into paths the user names.

## Resolve media pool

- Sources: `Master/video` (or equivalent).
- Timelines: **only** in `Master/timelines`.
- After creating a timeline, move its pool item into `timelines` if needed.

## Timeline naming

```
Reel NN - ShortLabel
```

Examples: `Reel 01 - Zachem hybrid`, `Reel 02 - Factory ARB`.

## Lock protocol

- Locked timelines: rename only if asked; never rebuild content.
- Experimental timelines may be deleted/rebuilt.
- Check `projects/<name>/notes/LOCKS.md`.

## Language / scope

- Talk to the user in Russian unless they switch.
- Theme-specific plot stays in `projects/<name>/`; knowledge/skills stay generic.
